herdr-app
=========

macOS app (Herdr.app) that shows spaces, tabs and panes. herdr-core (hc) runs the
terminals, on this Mac or on a remote machine. Separate from the herdr TUI: they share no
sessions. Default keys below. Full list: cmd-/ or herdr-app --skill.

SPACES AND TABS
  cmd-n                           New space
  cmd-t / cmd-w                   New / close tab
  ctrl-tab / ctrl-shift-tab       Next / previous tab
  cmd-shift-] / cmd-shift-[       Next / previous tab
  cmd-alt-] / cmd-alt-[           Next / previous space
  f2 / shift-f2                   Rename tab / space

PANES
  cmd-d / cmd-shift-d             Split right / down
  cmd-alt-<arrow>                 Focus the pane in that direction
  cmd-alt-shift-<arrow>           Swap with the pane in that direction
  cmd-shift-enter                 Zoom the pane
  cmd-shift-w                     Close the pane

AGENTS AND SEARCH
  cmd-] / cmd-[                   Next / previous agent
  cmd-p                           Picker
  cmd-shift-p                     Command palette (every command, with its key)
  cmd-f                           Find in the focused terminal

WINDOW
  cmd-b                           Toggle the sidebar
  cmd-shift-l                     Switch layout
  cmd-,                           Settings
  cmd-/                           Keys and help
  ctrl-alt-shift-escape           Escape hatch: default layout and keys

REMOTE MACHINES (run on the Mac)
  hc machine add <ssh-host> --name <name>
                                  Add a machine. Offers to copy hc there
  hc machine ls                   Machines and their state
  hc machine login <name>         Reconnect now (run mwinit first if auth expired)
  hc machine update <name>        Push a newer hc and restart it. Terminals keep running
  SSH to the machine must print nothing and must not ask for a PTY.

AGENTS FROM A SCRIPT OR AN AGENT
  hc run --bg --name <n> <agent> "<task>"
                                  Start an agent in the background
  hc send <n> "<text>"            Type into it
  hc read <n> --lines 60          Read its screen
  hc wait <n>                     Wait until it is done
  hc --skill                      Full manual for agents
  herdr-app do space.new --name <n> --folder <dir>
                                  Make a space (herdr-app commands lists all)
  Only agents that report status (Claude, Codex) show working, blocked or done.

SERVER (on the machine that runs hc)
  hc server status                Core state, pid, uptime
  echo $HC_TERMINAL_ID            Set inside an hc terminal. HERDR_ENV is not set

CONFIG
  ~/.config/herdr-app/settings.json
                                  App settings (also the Settings UI, cmd-,)
  ~/.config/herdr-app/keys.json   Keys. Editing it stops new default keys
  ~/.config/herdr-core/config.toml
                                  hc settings (optional, on the machine that runs hc)
